# A profile review document borrowing the component's vocabulary

The two legends say different things about different subjects. The component's `[MET]` is a claim
about a piece of evidence; a profile ledger's `[FULL]` is a claim about a milestone row's whole
exit gate. A reader who met `[MET]` in a profile ledger would have to guess which of the two
vocabularies it came from, and the guess would change what the row means.

| Verdict | Milestone | State |
|---|---|---|
| [MET] | **JS-4 — value representation and object model** | **Not started** |

- [UNMET] the row above, restated as a list item so the scan is shown reaching both forms.
